# Docker gets ONLY what git keeps (L16.2). On Tejas's PC this folder also holds .env (the bot's key), his personal
# files, 1 GB of price data, the live alerts' files and the old bot's key files - none of it may enter an image.
# So: leave out everything, let in the tracked folders and files, then leave out again what .gitignore leaves out.
*
!.github/
!.dockerignore
!.env.example
!.gitattributes
!.gitignore
!.gitleaksignore
!CLAUDE.md
!PRIVATE-PARTS.md
!Dockerfile
!README.md
!compose.yaml
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt
!requirements-live.txt
!requirements-search.txt
!requirements-eyes.txt
!docs/
!machine/
!old/
!plan/
!public/
!strategy/
!tests/
!data/usd_inr.csv
!data/swap.csv
!data/news/signs.csv
!data/news/dgs2.csv

# inside those, what .gitignore leaves out
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/*.tmp
**/*.joblib
**/*.pkl
**/*.npz
**/.env
**/*.env
**/mlruns
old/build/data
old/ml/data/fastbt*
old/ml/agent/agent_config.json
old/ml/agent/state.json
old/ml/agent/clock.json
old/ml/agent/logs
old/ml/logs
